tool.command:
## NFS root_squash: root in container → nobody on NFS, can't write to galaxy-owned workdir. groupadd -g 1001 gxgroup 2>/dev/null || true && useradd -M -u 1001 -g 1001 gxuser 2>/dev/null || true && export HOME=\$PWD/home && runuser -u gxuser -- bash -c "mkdir -p ./home/input ./home/output ./home/omero" && #if $infile: #for $filename in $infile: #if $filename.ext == 'spatialdata.zip': runuser -u gxuser -- bash -c "unzip -q '$filename' -d ./home/input/" && #else runuser -u gxuser -- bash -c "ln -s '$filename' './home/input/${filename.element_identifier}.${filename.ext}'" && #end if #end for #end if echo "Installed napari version:" && #if str($plugin) == 'spdata': echo "Installing napari-spatialdata and squidpy..." && /opt/conda/bin/conda run -n napari pip install napari-spatialdata squidpy && #end if ## /init calls mktemp; Galaxy sets TMPDIR=$CWD/tmp/ which root_squash blocks. Reset to /tmp. export TMPDIR=/tmp && ## Reconfigure container nginx for path-based proxy: EP_PATH_CLEAN="\${EP_PATH%/}" && sed -i "s|location ~ /websockify|location \${EP_PATH_CLEAN}/websockify {
 websockify_pass unix:/tmp/vnc.sock;
 websockify_read_timeout 5d;
 websockify_send_timeout 5d;
 }

 location \${EP_PATH_CLEAN} {
 alias /opt/noVNC/;
 index index.html;
 add_header Cache-Control no-cache;
 }

 location ~ /websockify|" /opt/base/etc/nginx/default_site.conf && /init

tool.help:
Napari is a Python library for n-dimensional image visualisation, annotation, and analysis. With napari you can:

    - view and explore 2D, 3D, and higher-dimensional arrays on a canvas;

    - overlay derived data such as points, polygons, segmentations, and more;

    - annotate and edit derived datasets, using standard data structures such as NumPy or Zarr arrays, allowing you to seamlessly weave exploration, computation, and annotation together in imaging data analysis.

**Note:** SpatialData should be provided as a zipped file with the spatialdata.zip format.
